Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The chapters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixways, while the company waits; the first Lullday it spends in the valley; the next; the Working Day. Each opens
  // on the first page that finds the company where it is told.
  Chapter ch_sixways "Sixways" when within(party, sixways) and not cameIn(party) "Six days of the week Sixways is a hamlet on the march with too many carts for its size, and the seventh it is a door. Everyone here lives by the Lull: they cart for it, buy its cloth, sell it what it will not make, marry into it, wait for it. They count its days on a board by the pump and a stone on the rise. They say of someone who has gone in and not come out for a long while that they are lingering, and they do not say it unkindly.".
  Chapter ch_first "The First Lullday" when cameIn(party) and dayOne() "It is the holy day. It has been the holy day in this valley for fifty-seven years, which is four hundred of the world's, and nobody you meet here has done anything today that they did not mean to. The road you came in by will be there until midnight.".
  Chapter ch_second "The Second Lullday" when dayTwo() and inLull(party) and not hesterDead(hester) "For the Lull it is the next morning. For you it is a week on, and you can see it in the way people look at you: the Lull-born notice a week on a face the way other people notice a haircut. The Long Table is being laid. The Weekday Club is on the broken bridge, talking low. The Working Day is the next Lullday.".
  Chapter ch_second_mourning "The Second Lullday" when dayTwo() and inLull(party) and hesterDead(hester) and not chapterOpened(ch_second) "For the Lull it is the next morning; for you, a week on. Somebody has tied a black thread to the top of the Strike Post. In the Gardens, people talk low over the beans. Hester Lindsell died in the night, and tonight is her Watching; the town says the wasting took her at last, and that it was a mercy, and some of them look at the Lindsells' door while they say it. The Working Day is the next Lullday.".
  Chapter ch_working "The Working Day" when dayThree() and inLull(party) and workingBegun(lull_country) "It is the Lullday. It is also, for the first time in fifty-seven years, something else. Before six the young of Linger went down to the Shift Bridge in their oldest clothes with ropes and timbers and a cart of stone, and when the town came out to lay the Long Table it found them working: in public, in daylight, with their sleeves rolled. Nobody is laying the Table. Everybody is going down to the leat.".
  Chapter ch_working_off "The Lullday After" when dayThree() and inLull(party) and not workingBegun(lull_country) "It is Lullday, as it always is. The Shift Bridge is broken, as it always has been, and nobody is on it. The Long Table is being laid.".
}
